### The interface

```ts
interface JobQueue {
  enqueueJob(type: string, payload: unknown): Promise<string>;
  dequeueJobs(limit: number): Promise<Job[]>;
  markDone(jobId: string): Promise<void>;
  markFailed(jobId: string, error: string): Promise<void>;
}
```

Every environment implements this same interface. Business code depends on `JobQueue`, never on MongoDB or Service Bus directly.

### Why the queue matters most

It's the only component that *must* change when infrastructure changes. Everything else (app code, UI, services) is portable. Get the abstraction right once, and the Vercel → Azure migration becomes an adapter swap.
